# Project Structure

Follow this layout. Do not invent alternate homes for these concerns.

| Concern | Path | Purpose |
|---------|------|---------|
| Config | `src/common/config/` | Env-backed Nest config (`configs/*.config.ts`, `config.type.ts`, `envs.ts`) |
| Infrastructure | `src/common/infrastructure/` | Persistence & other infra bridges (e.g. Prisma, `base.repository.ts`) |
| External libs | `src/common/libs/` | Third-party wiring (Pino, Swagger, i18n) |
| Shared DTO/utils | `src/common/dto/`, `src/common/utils/` | Cross-cutting helpers (`GetManyQuery`, `buildFindManyArgs`) |
| Domain modules | `src/modules/<domain>/` | Feature code only |

## Config pattern

- Add new settings under `src/common/config/configs/<name>.config.ts` with `registerAs`, Joi validation schema, and exported config type.
- Register the loader + schema in `AppModule` `ConfigModule.forRoot` and extend `Configs` in `config.type.ts`.

## Libs vs infrastructure

- **Libs**: wrap/configure an external package (logger, swagger UI).
- **Infrastructure**: app persistence/adapters that domain modules depend on (Prisma module/provider, generic `Repository`).

## Module folder layout

```
src/modules/<domain>/
  controllers/
  services/
  repositories/
  dto/request/
  dto/response/
  contracts/       # abstract API for other modules
  providers/       # implementations of contracts
  <domain>.module.ts
```
